    <name>
      <text>14.4 Find intercept of perpendicular</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Line <b>\(L\)</b> has equation \({@aa*y@} {@if bb>0 then "-" else "+"@} {@abs(bb)*x@} = {@cc@}\).</p>
<p>Line <b>\(M\)</b> goes through the point <i>\(A\)</i>\(({@dd@}, {@ee@})\) and the point <i>\(B\)</i>\(({@ff@}, k)\).</p>
<p><b>\(L\)</b> is perpendicular to <b>\(M\)</b>.<p>
<p>Follow these steps to find the value of \(k\):</p>
<p><br>Find the gradient of line <b>\(L\)</b>:</p>
<p align="right">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(1)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>Using the fact that it is perpendicular to line <b>\(L\)</b>, find the gradient of line <b>\(M\)</b>:</p>
<p align="right">[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(1)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>Write an equation involving \(k\) and solve it.</p>
<p align="right">\(k=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
